      "side": 1,
      "message": "True, if a plugin that requires an `ApiModule` is installed in a Gerrit setup without its prerequisites.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "3e0c45a9df6890d4a2933486c3e4f65aa5777f46",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02201854_83bc99ea",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-26T11:39:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s not true: Gerrit from v3.9 onwards assures that all `ApiModule` are loaded before all plugins.\n\nPlugins are then loaded into their sandboxed injectors and class loaders and do not see each other.\n\nThe problem here is different IMHO: a Gerrit admin may want to decide, because of its organisation of the rest of the pipeline, the order of generation of events, which is defined by the order of loading of the plugins.\n\nExample: if you load the `pull-replication.jar` and then the `multi-site.jar`, the ref updated event happens *after* the sync replication, therefore the CI/CD would see the change immediately without waits and the reindexing can happen without retries. If you load them in the inverted order, you may end up with failed builds and indexes could take more time to catch-up.\n\nIn the above example, even if the `multi-site.jar` and `pull-replication.jar` do not have direct class dependencies, they still need to be loaded in a very specific order at startup.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "3e0c45a9df6890d4a2933486c3e4f65aa5777f46",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "09fff5e6_7096d96c",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010134
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-26T13:24:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t that be a default behaviour of the `pull-replication` plugin when it\u0027s used with `multi-site`?\n\nI\u0027m not fond of admins resorting to renaming files (as this is error-prone and can be easily undone by other team members unknowingly). IMO the burden of such _cross-dependencies_ is on plugin authors. We should strive to provide API for them that makes those types of resolutions easy. IMO simply adding `Depends-On` and automatic plugin dependency resolution is not enough. We also need a mechanism to advertise that crucial parts of the plugin startup process are finished.",
      "parentUuid": "02201854_83bc99ea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "3e0c45a9df6890d4a2933486c3e4f65aa5777f46",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
